> - If you do not need to output Device Assistant tags, you can leave this parameter empty or do not pass it.', example='DeviceRisk', position='Query'),
  h5DegradeConfirmBtn?: string(name='H5DegradeConfirmBtn', description='Specifies whether to display the I Have Completed Authentication button on the H5 downgrade page after authentication is completed. Valid values:
- **Y**: Displays the button.
- **N** (default): Hides the button.', example='Y', position='Query'),
  ip?: string(name='Ip', description='The IP address of the user.', example='114.xxx.xxx.xxx', position='Query'),
  metaInfo?: string(name='MetaInfo', description='The Metainfo environment parameter. You must obtain this parameter by using the client SDK.', example='{"zimVer":"3.0.0","appVersion": "1","bioMetaInfo": "4.1.0:11501568,0","appName": "com.aliyun.antcloudauth","deviceType": "ios","osVersion": "iOS 10.3.2","apdidToken": "","deviceModel": "iPhone9,1"}', position='Query'),
  mobile?: string(name='Mobile', description='The mobile phone number of the user.', example='130xxxxxxxx', position='Query'),
  mode?: string(name='Mode', description='The method to obtain the passport NFC verification elements. Valid values:

- **1**: User input. The end user manually enters the ID document element information by using the UI provided by the Alibaba Cloud SDK.

- **3**: External parameter input. The ID document element information is passed from external sources.

> When the NFC decoder decrypts the encrypted information of the passport chip, it needs to obtain three passport elements: name, date of birth, and expiration date.', example='1', position='Query'),
  model?: string(name='Model', description='The liveness detection type. Valid values:
> Only the following liveness detection types are supported. Custom actions or combinations are not supported.

Description
Only the following liveness detection types are supported. Custom actions or combinations are not supported.

- **LIVENESS** (default): Blinking.

- **PHOTINUS_LIVENESS**: Blinking and colorful light reflection.

- **MULTI_ACTION**: Blinking and head turning (the order is random).

- **MOVE_ACTION** (recommended): Moving closer or farther and blinking.

- **MOVE_PHOTINUS**: Moving closer or farther and colorful light reflection.

> 
>- **The default liveness detection type** is supported in the following SDK versions:
>   - Android SDK 1.2.6 and later
>   - iOS SDK 1.2.4 and later
>   - Harmony SDK 1.0.0 and later
>- Other types are supported in the latest SDK versions for Android, iOS, and Harmony. We recommend that you integrate the latest SDK version.', example='MOVE_ACTION', position='Body'),
  needMultiFaceCheck?: string(name='NeedMultiFaceCheck', description='Specifies whether to intercept the request when multiple faces are detected on the terminal. Valid values:

- **Y**: Intercepts the request. The client prompts the user to scan the face again.

- **N** (default): Does not intercept the request. The largest face in the face scanning screen is sent to the server for security detection.', example='Y', position='Query'),
  ossBucketName?: string(name='OssBucketName', description='The name of the authorized OSS bucket.

> You can specify only one of the following parameters to pass the image: FaceContrastPicture, FaceContrastPictureUrl, CertifyId, and OSS.', example='cn-shanghai-aliyun-cloudauth-xxxxx', position='Query'),
  ossObjectName?: string(name='OssObjectName', description='The name of the object in the authorized OSS bucket.

> You can specify only one of the following parameters to pass the image: FaceContrastPicture, FaceContrastPictureUrl, CertifyId, and OSS.', example='verify/xxxxx/xxxxxx.jpeg', position='Query'),
  outerOrderNo?: string(name='OuterOrderNo', description='The unique identifier of the merchant request.

The value is a 32-character alphanumeric string. The first few characters are a custom abbreviation of the merchant, the middle part can be a period of time, and the last part can be a random or incremental sequence.', example='e0c34a77f5ac40a5aa5e6ed20c353888', position='Query'),
  procedurePriority?: string(name='ProcedurePriority', description='The downgrade configuration when WebRTC or WebAssembly is incompatible during mobile H5 authentication. Valid values:

- **keep**: Downgrade is not supported. The result is directly returned.

- **url** (default): Downgrade is supported. The authentication URL is returned. The user opens or switches to a browser by using this URL for authentication.

- **video**: Downgrade is supported. The system camera is used to record a 3- to 5-second blinking video for authentication.


> 
> When the downgrade mode is set to video, the following features become invalid and product security is reduced. We recommend that you configure this mode only for security scenarios.
> - The liveness detection type setting does not take effect.
> - The VideoEvidence feature is not supported.', example='url', position='Query'),
  productCode?: string(name='ProductCode', description='The fixed value. The value of this parameter varies based on the product solution:
- APP authentication solution: Set the value to ID_PRO.
- Face liveness verification solution: Set the value to PV_FV.
- Liveness detection solution: Set the value to LR_FR.', example='ID_PRO', position='Query'),
  rarelyCharacters?: string(name='RarelyCharacters', description='Specifies whether to enable the rare character mode. Valid values:

- **Y**: Enables the mode. Before authentication, an information input box appears. The user must enter the name with rare characters and the ID card number, and agree to the agreement before the authentication process starts.

- **N**: Does not enable the mode. This is the default value.', example='Y', position='Query'),
  readImg?: string(name='ReadImg', description='Specifies whether to read the ID document photo. Valid values:

- **Y**: Reads the photo.

- **N**: Does not read the photo.

> If you need to use the face photo from the ID document in subsequent authentication steps, we recommend that you set this parameter to Y.', example='Y', position='Query'),
  returnUrl?: string(name='ReturnUrl', description='The redirect URL for the merchant business page.', example='www.aliyun.com', position='Query'),
  sceneId?: long(name='SceneId', description='The ID of the authentication scenario.', example='1000000006', position='Query'),
  suitableType?: string(name='SuitableType', description='The age-friendly configuration parameter. This parameter takes effect for each authentication request. You can select different parameters for each authentication request based on the business property, customer distribution, and operation attribute of your app. The following options are available. Default value: 0.

- **0**: Disables the age-friendly pattern for the current authentication request.

- **1**: Enables the age-friendly pattern for the current authentication request.

- **2**: Allows the user to select the pattern.


The end user can select the authentication pattern. The product guide page provides two authentication entries: Start Authentication and Senior Authentication Pattern. When the user selects Senior Authentication Pattern, the system enters the age-friendly pattern.
> 
> - The age-friendly parameter takes effect only when the liveness detection type **Model** is set to **LIVENESS** or **MULTI_ACTION**.', example='0', position='Query'),
  uiCustomUrl?: string(name='UiCustomUrl', description='The URL of the UI configuration file.

For the complete configuration, see [Web SDK UI custom configuration](https://www.alibabacloud.com/help/en/id-verification/financial-grade-id-verification/web-sdk-ui-custom-configuration-description).', example='www.aliyundoc.com', position='Query'),
  userId?: string(name='UserId', description='The custom user ID in the customer business. Make sure that the ID is unique.', example='123456789', position='Query'),
  validityDate?: string(name='ValidityDate', description='The expiration date of the ID document.

This parameter is required when the **CertType** parameter is set to **PASSPORT** and the **Mode** parameter is set to **3**.', example='2039-06-10', position='Query'),
  videoEvidence?: string(name='VideoEvidence', description='Specifies whether to enable video evidence. Valid values:

- **true**: Enables video evidence.

- **false**: Does not enable video evidence. This is the default value.

> Because video files are large, the system discards video files to prioritize the transmission of necessary authentication images when the network is unstable. We recommend that you set your business to weakly depend on videos.', example='false', position='Query'),
  voluntaryCustomizedContent?: string(name='VoluntaryCustomizedContent', description='The custom willingness content. This parameter is required when personalized settings are enabled. The value is a JSON string of a string list.

- In the read-along scenario: The content cannot exceed 60 Chinese characters (excluding punctuation marks), and the list contains only one element.

- In the Q&A scenario: You can configure up to three questions. Each question cannot exceed 30 Chinese characters, and each question is an element in the list.', example='["I, Mr. Wang, agree to the *** agreement."]', position='Query'),
}

model InitFaceVerifyResponseBody = {
  code?: string(name='Code', description='The return code. A value of 200 indicates success, and other values indicate failure.', example='200'),
  message?: string(name='Message', description='The error message.', example='success'),
  requestId?: string(name='RequestId', description='The request ID.', example='130A2C10-B9EE-4D84-88E3-5384FF039795'),
  resultObject?: {
    certifyId?: string(name='CertifyId', description='The unique identifier of ID Verification.', example='91707dc296d469ad38e4c5efa6a0f24b'),
    certifyUrl?: string(name='CertifyUrl', description='The URL for ID Verification in a web browser. After the authentication is completed, the user is redirected based on the ReturnUrl parameter.

>Notice: 

- The CertifyUrl returned by the initialization API operation is **valid for 30 minutes and can be used to submit authentication only once**. Use it within the validity period to avoid repeated use.
- This parameter requires the correct input of the **MetaInfo** parameter to return a CertifyUrl that matches the client. If you cannot obtain it, check whether **MetaInfo** and other input parameters are correct.

- The domain name of this URL may change with service updates. To ensure normal service availability, we recommend that you do not configure access control for this domain name.

- When the browser redirects, try not to use incognito mode or change the URL. Otherwise, a **signature exception** error may occur.', example='https://t.aliyun.com/****'),
  }(name='ResultObject', description='The result object.'),
}

model InitFaceVerifyResponse = {
  headers?: map[string]string(name='headers'),
  statusCode?: int32(name='statusCode'),
  body?: InitFaceVerifyResponseBody(name='body'),
}

/**
  * @description - Endpoint: cloudauth.aliyuncs.com
  * - Request method: HTTPS POST and GET.
  * - This API operation uses different parameters for different product solutions. For more information, see [official documentation](https://www.alibabacloud.com/help/en/id-verification/financial-grade-id-verification/product-overview/introduction/).
  * #### Image format requirements
  * When you perform ID Verification, make sure that the uploaded image meets all the following conditions:
  * - The photo is recent, the face is complete, clear, and unobstructed, the expression is natural, and the face is directly facing the camera.
  * - The photo is clear and properly exposed. The face is not too dark, too bright, or surrounded by halos. The angle does not have significant deviation.
  * - The resolution does not exceed 1920×1080 and is at least 640×480. We recommend that you scale the short side to 720 pixels and set the compression ratio to greater than 0.9.
  * - Image size: less than 1 MB.
  * - Photos rotated by 90, 180, or 270 degrees are supported. If multiple faces are detected, the largest face is selected.
  * @param request  the request parameters of InitFaceVerify  InitFaceVerifyRequest
  * @return InitFaceVerifyResponse
 */
async function initFaceVerify(request: InitFaceVerifyRequest): InitFaceVerifyResponse {
  @handler.validateRequestModel(request);
  return @handler.do('RPC', 'InitFaceVerify', 'POST', '/', 'json', true, 'form', request);
}

